# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# SEAT AIRLINES
#
# There is no simulator any more. With nothing set, the instruments hold the
# opening reading (INITIAL_TICK in src/lib/flightFeed.ts) and never move,
# because the feed has no URL to poll — the aircraft is parked, not pretending.
# Set these to point it at a real token.
#
# Note that the mint does NOT normally belong here. It is committed, in
# src/lib/token.ts, so that going live is a one-line change that reviews and
# deploys like any other. VITE_TOKEN_MINT overrides it, for a fork or a
# staging deployment pointed somewhere else.
#
# In CI these are repository *variables*, not secrets: Vite inlines every
# VITE_-prefixed value into the bundle it ships, so storing one as a secret
# hides it from the repository and from nobody else.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# ── The token ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The SPL mint the aircraft is flying. Overrides the committed value in
# src/lib/token.ts. Set either one and the market feed starts polling
# Jupiter's free public API.
VITE_TOKEN_MINT=

# Your Solana RPC. A public endpoint will rate-limit a busy page — use your
# own. Required for balances and the seat ladder.
VITE_RPC_URL=

# ── The manifest ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# An endpoint returning [{ "address": "...", "balance": 123 }, ...], richest
# first.
#
# This is not really optional. Without it the code falls back to the RPC's
# getTokenLargestAccounts, which returns at most 20 accounts — and the cabin
# seats 40. Half the aeroplane would sit empty no matter how many holders
# the token has.
VITE_HOLDERS_URL=

# ── Market data ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Jupiter's keyless endpoint is the default and needs nothing set here.
#
# Override to use a keyed plan or your own indexer. Anything returning JSON
# with market cap, a five-minute price change and a holder count will do —
# the parser finds market cap and holders by field name, and the change by
# locating the 5m window first (every window Jupiter returns has a field
# called priceChange, so the name alone is ambiguous).
# VITE_MARKET_URL=

# ── The advertising wall ─────────────────────────────────────────────────
# The advert server (see worker/). With this set, holders publish their own
# adverts, signed by their wallet, and everyone sees the same wall. Without
# it an upload stays in the uploader's browser and the dialog says so.
VITE_BANNERS_API=

# A curated, read-only wall keyed by seat: { "<seat>": { image, alt, href } }.
# Independent of the above, and wins over it — use it to pin house creative.
# VITE_BANNERS_URL=

# ── The cabin ────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# How many seats the manifest fills, capped at the number the cabin has.
# Defaults to 40, which is the whole aeroplane. Lower it only to test what a
# partly-sold cabin looks like.
# VITE_MANIFEST_SIZE=
